review_comments:
I think you could mostly eliminate this method if you did something like:
```C#
options ??= JsonSerializerOptions.Default;
var jsonTypeInfo = (JsonTypeInfo<TValue>)options.GetTypeInfo(typeof(TValue));
FromJsonStreamAsyncCore(...,jsonTypeInfo,...); // the JsonTypeInfo overload.
```

To ensure consistent semantics with `JsonSerializer`, we should also lock the `options` instance ahead of resolving the `JsonTypeInfo`:
```suggestion
            options ??= JsonSerializerOptions.Default;
            options.MakeReadOnly();
```
